<Project>

    <!--
        Build firewall — DO NOT add <Import> of the repository-root Directory.Build.props.

        This file stops MSBuild's upward Directory.Build.props discovery at this folder, so a quarantined
        tree does not inherit the engine's build context from the repository root. Moving a tree out of
        src/ does not remove it from MSBuild's reach: the root props walk DOWN into experimental/ exactly
        as readily as into src/, because the walk is upward from each project and nothing stopped it here.
        The architecture gate makes that concrete — hooked at the root, it would run on a project
        deliberately removed from the graph and judge it against a ledger that cannot describe it.

        QUARANTINE MEANS UNGATED, and this pair is what makes that structural rather than a path filter
        someone maintains. A filter that happens to exclude the right directories reads identically to one
        that excludes the wrong ones.

        Nothing here is built by the root build or listed in Puck.slnx. Anything in this tree that must
        keep working belongs in a real project or a `puck` verb, not here.
    -->

</Project>
